# b770 -- THE ACT`S SECTIONS OF THE SEVEN CLOSE TOOLS ((R380)(2)(i), tools/standing/fold.py), READ AS TEXT, NOT IMPORTED.
# Each block opens with a line "#⟪SECTION <tool> <n>⟫" (the act`s own lines, verbatim, at the template`s slot n of that tool)
# or "#⟪OVERRIDE <tool> <first> <last>⟫" (the act`s lines in place of the template`s lines first..last) and closes with the line
# "#⟪END⟫"; " NOEOL" before the closing mark: the last line has no newline; " REPAIR <name>" after an override names the
# (R380)(2) repair it carries. Edited by the Edit tool. Carried at b770 by tools/b770_fold.py (`carry`) from tools/acts/b769.py,
# b769`s names substituted; the citation`s sections adopted from tools/b770_citation.py as landed (`adopt citation`).
# Each "#⟪DEAD <tool> <names>⟫" line: the names the act`s tool reads through its worklist alias that the worklist lacks, on
# routes the act never ran (b769`s dead routes, carried); the loader prints them and refuses any other missing name.
# Each "#⟪PENDING <tool> <names>⟫" line: the names the act has still to write (its own arms and figures, b769`s carried till
# then); the loader prints them at every load, and the seal wants every PENDING line empty.
